<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rafael Urdaneta</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1788–1845</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rafael Urdaneta was a Venezuelan general of the wars of independence and a close ally of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-bolivar">Simón Bolívar</a>. He served as minister of war of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/esztergom">Gran</a> Colombia and in September 1830 seized power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bogota">Bogotá</a>, hoping to recall Bolívar. After Bolívar's death his regime collapsed in 1831. He later held office in Venezuela and died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rafael-urdaneta.jpg" alt="Rafael Urdaneta" width="320" height="355" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Martín Tovar y Tovar · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rafael_urdaneta.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
